From: Elevator HMI meta-hmi-platform
Subject: [PATCH] drm: panel: jadard — LMT101SX006C final reset sequence (vendor Q1)

With GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW in the DTS, gpiod_set_value(1) drives XRES physically LOW
(asserted) and gpiod_set_value(0) drives it physically HIGH (deasserted).

The 3-step sequence inherited from patch 0002 (cz101b4001, GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH)
produces the wrong physical order: LOW(5ms) → HIGH(20ms) → LOW(120ms) → MIPI.
XRES is still asserted when jadard_enable() fires; the panel cannot respond.

Vendor Q1 (authoritative): Power On → 10ms → XRES LOW → 20ms → XRES HIGH →
120ms → MIPI commands.

Fix: collapse to the two-step sequence that matches Q1 exactly.
Physical result: HIGH(init) → 10ms → LOW(20ms) → HIGH(120ms) → MIPI.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
@@ -172,14 +172,11 @@ static int jadard_prepare(struct drm_panel *panel)

 	if (jadard->reset) {
 		gpiod_set_value(jadard->reset, 1);
-		msleep(5);
-
-		gpiod_set_value(jadard->reset, 0);
-		msleep(20); /* vendor spec: 20ms XRES pulse width */
-
-		gpiod_set_value(jadard->reset, 1);
-		msleep(jadard->desc->post_reset_delay ?
-		       jadard->desc->post_reset_delay : 5);
+		msleep(20); /* vendor Q1: XRES active-low, 20 ms pulse */
+
+		gpiod_set_value(jadard->reset, 0);
+		msleep(jadard->desc->post_reset_delay ?
+		       jadard->desc->post_reset_delay : 5);
 	} else {
 		/* Allow rail ramp when XRES is not under software control. */
 		msleep(135);
